1:1 COMMENT "# typed_data.z -- data blocks with explicit element type via `out T`."
1:70 EOL "\n"
2:1 COMMENT "#"
2:2 EOL "\n"
3:1 COMMENT "# A data block has ONE element type, settled where it is written:"
3:66 EOL "\n"
4:1 COMMENT "#   - `data { ... } out T`      the clause names it"
4:52 EOL "\n"
5:1 COMMENT "#   - `data { 1.u8 2 3 }`       the elements' own tags name it, and must agree"
5:79 EOL "\n"
6:1 COMMENT "#   - `data { ... }`            neither: i64, or f64 when every element is a"
6:77 EOL "\n"
7:1 COMMENT "#                               bare float literal"
7:51 EOL "\n"
8:1 COMMENT "#"
8:2 EOL "\n"
9:1 COMMENT "# A value the chosen type cannot hold is an error at the declaration, not a"
9:76 EOL "\n"
10:1 COMMENT "# truncation at each read."
10:27 EOL "\n"
11:1 COMMENT "#"
11:2 EOL "\n"
12:1 COMMENT "# When the block is a constant lookup table of bytes / small ints,"
12:67 EOL "\n"
13:1 COMMENT "# `out u8` keeps the C-level array narrow (one byte per slot"
13:61 EOL "\n"
14:1 COMMENT "# instead of eight) without forcing per-element `.u8` suffixes."
14:64 EOL "\n"
15:1 EOL "\n"
16:1 COMMENT "# Typed: every element pinned to u8. The C emitter lays this out"
16:65 EOL "\n"
17:1 COMMENT "# as `static const uint8_t[]`."
17:31 EOL "\n"
18:1 LABEL "bytemask"
18:9 COLON ":"
18:10 WS " "
18:11 DATA "data"
18:15 WS " "
18:16 BRACEOPEN "{"
18:17 EOL "\n"
19:1 WS "    "
19:5 LABEL "LOW"
19:8 COLON ":"
19:9 WS " "
19:10 REFID "0"
19:11 EOL "\n"
20:1 WS "    "
20:5 LABEL "MID"
20:8 COLON ":"
20:9 WS " "
20:10 REFID "64"
20:12 EOL "\n"
21:1 WS "    "
21:5 LABEL "HIGH"
21:9 COLON ":"
21:10 WS " "
21:11 REFID "250"
21:14 EOL "\n"
22:1 BRACECLOSE "}"
22:2 WS " "
22:3 OUT "out"
22:6 WS " "
22:7 REFID "u8"
22:9 EOL "\n"
23:1 EOL "\n"
24:1 COMMENT "# No clause and no tags: the elements are i64."
24:47 EOL "\n"
25:1 EOL "\n"
26:1 LABEL "primes"
26:7 COLON ":"
26:8 WS " "
26:9 DATA "data"
26:13 WS " "
26:14 BRACEOPEN "{"
26:15 WS " "
26:16 REFID "2"
26:17 WS " "
26:18 REFID "3"
26:19 WS " "
26:20 REFID "5"
26:21 WS " "
26:22 REFID "7"
26:23 WS " "
26:24 REFID "11"
26:26 WS " "
26:27 BRACECLOSE "}"
26:28 EOL "\n"
27:1 EOL "\n"
28:1 COMMENT "# Tagged elements: `1.u8` types the whole block, so this is `out u8`"
28:69 EOL "\n"
29:1 COMMENT "# written the other way round, down to the C array."
29:52 EOL "\n"
30:1 LABEL "masked"
30:7 COLON ":"
30:8 WS " "
30:9 DATA "data"
